Research Associate in Nonlinear Array Enabled Wireless Security
Edinburgh, Midlothian, United Kingdom

Role:&nbsp;
Research Associate in Nonlinear Array Enabled Wireless Security

Grade and Salary:
 Grade 7 (£38,448 - £46,970) per annum

FTE and working pattern:
 1 FTE (full-time, 35 hours per week) fixed term until March 2030

Holiday Entitlement:
 33 days annual leave&nbsp;plus 9 buildings-closed days (and Christmas Eve when it falls on a weekday). Use our total rewards calculator:&nbsp;

 

https://www.hw.ac.uk/about/work/total-rewards-calculator.htm

 

to see the value of benefits provided by Heriot-Watt University

&nbsp;

Purpose of Role

We are seeking candidates with a record that will demonstrate their capability to effectively deliver the required research activities.&nbsp;&nbsp;

You will have a strong academic track record with knowledge and experience in the area of radio communications, RF and wireless systems, as well as the various software defined radio options. You will be competent in microwave and wireless system development and testing. You will also be experienced in nonlinear RF characterisation and signal processing algorithms. You will also be prepared to work on interfacing radio, digital and mechanical equipment to integrate fully functional multi-antenna transceivers at FR3.&nbsp;

The project will involve regular progress meetings with researchers, industrial partners as well as other collaborators, including PhD students in the group. You will be an effective communicator capable of hosting meetings. There is a number of milestones, and you will be expected to have excellent project management skills in delivering those. You will be responsible for the preparation of reports, minutes of meeting and other deliverable items required for the project. You will also be expected to author high-quality publications and present your results in scientific and industrial audiences.&nbsp;

This opportunity therefore relates to high-quality, self-motivated individuals with the ability to work and actively participate in developing advanced research in electromagnetics, microwave and antenna engineering and expanding the teaching knowledge base within the School’s Electrical, Electronic &amp; Computer Engineering disciplines.&nbsp;

For an informal discussion regarding this position, please contact Dr Yuan Ding. Email:&nbsp;

yuan.ding@hw.ac.uk

&nbsp;&nbsp;

For more information, please visit:&nbsp;

https://microwaves.site.hw.ac.uk/

&nbsp;

Key Duties &amp; Responsibilities

To review, design, implement and test the microwave modules and integrate them for active transmit and receive arrays.&nbsp;

To operate and adapt software defined radios for complete end-to-end wireless systems.

To operate microwave simulation and design software (ADS, CST, Matlab) and the equipment (VNA, VSA, VSG, loadpulling, etc.).

To undertake research into the analysis of physical-layer wireless communication system including novel antenna arrays, beamforming networks, as well as digital baseband algorithms for waveform generation.

To compile written reports and articles suitable for publication and contract fulfilment on the techniques, designs developed and results obtained.

Present regular progress reports on research to members of the research group or to external audiences to disseminate and publicise research findings.

Attend national and international meetings as required by the project.

Write up results of own work and contribute to the production of research reports, publications and funding proposals.

Read academic papers, journals, textbooks, attend specified training courses in order to keep abreast of developments.

Carry out any other duties designated by line manager and which fall within the general ambit of the post.

Please note that this job description is not exhaustive, and the role holder may be required to undertake other relevant duties commensurate with the grading of the post.&nbsp; Activities may be subject to amendment over time as the role develops and/or priorities and requirements evolve.&nbsp;

Essential &amp; Desirable Criteria

Essential

PhD Degree or equivalent in Electrical and Electronic Engineering, Physics or subject relevant to research activity.

Good understanding of microwave networks, antennas, nonlinear active devices and wireless communication systems.&nbsp;

Practical experience of applying the specialist skills and techniques required (including programming and software defined radios) for wireless communication systems.&nbsp;

Experience in writing high-quality academic papers and/or technical notes and reports.&nbsp;

Effective communication, report preparation, time management to meet deadlines.&nbsp;

Flexibility to travel for meetings.

Must be prepared to work as part of a team.

Ability to contribute to method improvement where required.&nbsp;

Desirable

Experience with implementation of end to end wireless communication links using digital and RF modules.

A minimum of one years’ relevant experience / track record of microwave devices and subsystems design.

Experience of software defined radios and RFSoC.

How to Apply

Applications can be submitted up to 11:55pm&nbsp;(UK time)&nbsp;on&nbsp;Tuesday 24th November 2026.

Please&nbsp;submit your CV &amp; covering letter via the Heriot-Watt on-line recruitment.

We may close this vacancy early if we receive a high volume of applications. We therefore encourage you to submit your application promptly.

We recognise that many candidates use AI tools during the application process and are comfortable with AI being used as a supporting aid. However, we want to hear from you, not AI.

Your application should be an authentic representation of your skills, experience and achievements. Applications that appear to have been fully generated by AI may not accurately reflect your suitability for the role and are therefore discouraged.

At interview, candidates will be expected to discuss and provide evidence of the experience, skills and examples included in their application.

We welcome and will consider flexible working patterns e.g., part-time working and job share options.

Heriot-Watt&nbsp;University is committed to securing equality of opportunity in employment and to the creation of an environment in which individuals are selected, trained, promoted, appraised, and otherwise treated on the sole basis of their relevant merits and abilities.&nbsp;Equality and diversity are all about maximising potential and creating a culture of inclusion for all.

Heriot-Watt&nbsp;University values diversity across our university community and welcomes applications from all sectors of society, particularly from underrepresented groups. For more information, please see our website&nbsp;

https://www.hw.ac.uk/uk/services/equality-diversity.htm

&nbsp;and also our award-winning work in Disability Inclusive Science Careers&nbsp;

https://disc.hw.ac.uk/

&nbsp;.

Use our total rewards calculator:&nbsp;

https://www.hw.ac.uk/about/work/total-rewards-calculator.htm

&nbsp;to see the value of benefits provided by Heriot-Watt University.

About the Team

The Microwave and Antenna Engineering Group at Heriot-Watt University is delivering world-leading research and engineering work in physical-layer of wireless systems, including satellite communications, cellular broadband, low-power electronics, and signal processing required for various wireless applications. This team on average secures multi-million pounds projects, and collaborating with many universities and industries worldwide. The group, led by Dr Yuan Ding, is pioneering the research on physical-layer wireless security, ambient backscatter communications, retrodirective arrays, and PNT related topics.&nbsp;

About Heriot-Watt University

At Heriot-Watt we are passionate about our values and look to them to connect our people globally and to help us collaborate and celebrate our success through working together. Our research programmes can deliver real world impact which is achieved through the diversity of our international community and the recognition of creative talent that connects our global team.

Our flourishing community will give you the freedom to challenge and to bring your enterprising mind and to help our partners with solutions that can be applied now and in the future. Join us and Heriot Watt will provide you with a platform to thrive and work in a way that also helps you live your life in balance with well-being and inclusiveness at the heart of our global community.

Research Assistant
Edinburgh - BioQuarter, Midlothian, United Kingdom

